  "method": "All 11,950 KEGG organism genomes (10,148 Bacteria, 469 Archaea, 1,333 Eukaryotes per BRITE br08601) were scored for presence of the 20 pre-registered marker families using KEGG REST link/genes/ko for each KO. 96.9% of genomes carry >= 18 of 20 markers (Bacteria 97.0%, Archaea 96.0%, Eukaryotes 96.3%); 83.8% carry all 20. The pre-registered rule nevertheless returns 'refutes' because the AspRS marker (K01876) is found in only 1.5% of Archaea: KEGG files the archaeal (and many bacterial) non-discriminating aspartyl-tRNA synthetase under a different orthology id, K09759. A post-hoc sensitivity analysis pooling K09759 into AspRS was added and is labelled as such in analysis.py and measured.extra; under it AspRS prevalence in Archaea is 87.4% and the only other marker below the 90% universality threshold is CysRS in Archaea (87.6%), giving 'mixed' under the pre-registered support rule.",
